# .forge/conformance/b2-ra-conformance-roundtrip — the class x surface x test-id matrix.
#
# Forge-skill conformance doctrine: TAB-separated rows of class<TAB>surface<TAB>evidence.
# evidence is either a red-capable test id/name (a unique substring of a test name in
# test/bounded_authority_report_adapter/conformance_roundtrip_test.exs), OR `n/a: <falsifiable reason>`.
# The conformance-verify.sh runner parses this matrix, confirms each evidence phrase
# appears in the test file, and re-executes the suite.
#
# Surfaces (from .forge/conformance-surfaces): the conformance harness exercises BAP's
# `check_envelope/2` (envelope verifier) and `verify_grant/3` (grant-only verifier, for the
# grant_time_cases which carry no proof).
#
# Classes are a genuine SELECTION from BAP's 16-class corpus taxonomy
# (deps/bounded_authority_protocol/test/conformance/corpus_test.exs:191-210), not a
# spec-named obligation on this adapter.
#
# TAB-separated: class	surface	evidence
valid	check_envelope	top-level grant+proof verify green
valid	check_envelope	received_member_order_variant grant+proof verify green
valid	check_envelope	nonce_absent verifies green
valid	check_envelope	an envelope signed through the adapter verifies green
invalid_key	check_envelope	wrong_holder goes red
invalid_duplicate	check_envelope	duplicate_member goes red
invalid_selector	check_envelope	selector_denied.equals goes red
invalid_selector	check_envelope	selector_denied.one_of goes red
tamper_meaningful_byte	check_envelope	flipped proof-signature byte goes RED
tamper_meaningful_byte	check_envelope	tampered ba_req payload byte goes RED at the request-hash field binding
tamper_meaningful_byte	check_envelope	tamper_verdicts all go RED through check_envelope
valid	verify_grant	every grant_time_case matches its declared expected_verdict
invalid_time	verify_grant	every grant_time_case matches its declared expected_verdict
